# `contracts` and `front` are NOT ignored, and the reason is one line in the build
# stage: `abis.test.ts` scans contracts/, contracts/interfaces, contracts/libraries,
# offchain/src AND front/src
# to assert that every name the off-chain code references is still declared
# on-chain, and which of the two TypeScript packages references it. It is the
# check that catches an ABI the contracts have moved on from, it runs inside
# `pnpm test`, and `pnpm test` gates the image.
#
# Excluding it did not skip the check — it made the build fail, first on
# `ENOENT scandir /app/contracts`, then `"/contracts": not found` once the COPY
# was added, then the same pair for front/src. Both reach the BUILD stage only:
# the runtime stage copies node_modules, offchain and the root manifest, so
# neither a .sol nor a line of the front ships in the image the keeper runs.
